---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy notice" description="How Wunder Tutor handles recordings, photo reading, account sync, teacher voices and optional reminders, and where to find your controls.">
  <article class="wrap privacy-article">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice · Updated 25 September 2026</p>
    <h1>Your voice and learning data.</h1>
    <p class="hero-lead">This notice describes the current Wunder Tutor beta, including optional accounts, recording contributions and reminders.</p>
    <section><h2>Microphone and pronunciation scoring</h2><p>You start recording with the microphone control. Recording stops when you finish, tap to stop or reach the recording limit. With real scoring enabled, a short clip and the expected phrase go through our API to Microsoft Azure Speech for assessment. The app receives pronunciation scores and feedback. Any result labelled simulated is not a real assessment.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Replay recordings and contributions</h2><p>The “Keep recordings on this device” setting lets you replay recent takes. These recordings are stored locally, separately from scores, and are not included in account sync.</p><p><b>“Help improve Wunder Tutor” is a separate choice and starts enabled for new setups.</b> When enabled, the team can keep practice recordings without a name, with assessment information, to test and improve pronunciation checks. Contributions are stored for up to 90 days. A device identifier allows the service to process deletion requests. You can turn this setting off during setup or in Settings.</p><p>Deleting recordings in the app removes local replay audio and requests deletion of that device’s contributed recordings. Use the deletion controls as well as switching contributions off if you want earlier contributions removed. Server actions require a working connection.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Teacher voices</h2><p>Text to be spoken is sent to the chosen cloud voice service, which may be Google Chirp, Qwen or Microsoft Azure. The app has primary and backup choices for each course; a backup may be tried if the primary cannot play. Some internal speech features still use Google Gemini. Device speech uses the device’s available speech engine.</p><p>Reusable lesson audio can be cached. Personal Notebook text is excluded from the shared lesson-audio cache. Pronunciation recordings are not sent to teacher-voice services to generate model speech.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Photos and Notebook text</h2><p>When you ask the app to read a photo, that image is sent through our API to Google Gemini to extract English or Chinese sentences. Typed Chinese text also uses the service to prepare characters and pinyin. Typed English can be split into sentences locally.</p><p>Wunder Tutor does not retain the photo in its reading service or account sync. Extracted or typed page text is saved in your browser and can be synced to your account if signed in. Provider processing follows the provider’s service terms. Avoid submitting sensitive material you do not want processed.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Local profiles and optional accounts</h2><p>Local browser storage holds a learner’s nickname, avatar, age group, preferences, course progress, scores, review history and saved page text. Clearing browser data can remove this local information.</p><p>If you sign in, the account service stores the sign-in email and can sync learner information, settings, progress, scores and saved page text. Account data is hosted with Supabase. Photos and replay recordings are not synced with the account. Recording contributions are a separate setting described above.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Optional reminders and shared scores</h2><p>Push reminders start off. Enabling them stores this browser’s push subscription, the chosen schedule, course choices and recent practice dates on the server. Reminder delivery does not need learner names or voice recordings. Abandoned reminder registrations are removed after 30 days.</p><p>Tongue-twister leaderboards show an avatar, a generated handle, a two-letter region and the result. They do not display the learner’s profile name, email or recording. Review the score-sharing control in Settings.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Hosting and providers</h2><p>Cloudflare hosts the website, app and API, including contributed-recording storage, reusable teacher audio and reminder infrastructure. Hosting and service providers process request information needed to deliver and protect their services. The website loads fonts from Google Fonts, so the browser contacts Google to request those files.</p><p>The app and site do not include advertising or third-party analytics scripts. This does not mean that hosting, font or speech providers receive no request data.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Your controls</h2><p>Open <b>Profile → Parent Zone</b> for children and teens, or <b>Profile → Settings & privacy</b> for adults. Settings opens directly; it is not protected by a separate adult verification gate. A parent or guardian should help children review the choices.</p><p>You can turn local replay storage and recording contributions on or off; delete recordings, pronunciation history or a profile; or delete the signed-in account and its saved data. Reminders can be paused or turned off in Reminders & rewards. Read each confirmation because the controls remove different data.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Questions</h2><p>For privacy questions, contact <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email}>{SITE.email}</a>. You can use the in-app deletion controls without sending an email.</p></section>
    <a class="text-link" href="/">← Back to Wunder Tutor</a>
  </article>
</Base>
